// buzzer.hjson
//
// Task 3D.1: defines the "Buzzer" enemy unit type - Tier 1 flying, per
// mod-units.md. Small flying unit, low health, short-range acid spit,
// spawns in swarms of 2-3. Triggered by "any active mining noise" - same
// trigger tier as Skitter, per the Escalation Summary table.
//
// This file reuses everything confirmed while building skitter.hjson,
// rather than re-discovering the same facts:
//   - Top-level "type" must be one of flying/mech/legs/naval/payload/
//     missile/tether/crawl (confirmed via a live IllegalArgument error
//     on skitter.hjson). "flying" is one of the confirmed-valid values,
//     just not one we'd used yet.
//   - Weapon has NO "range" field (confirmed via a live warning on
//     skitter.hjson) - omitted from the start here instead of
//     discovering it the same way twice.
//   - weapons[].bullet's polymorphic "type: BasicBulletType" syntax is
//     confirmed valid (skitter.hjson loads clean using it).
//   - Core UnitType fields (speed, hitSize, health, armor, accel, drag,
//     rotateSpeed, targetGround, targetAir, faceTarget, itemCapacity)
//     are confirmed via the official wiki's UnitType field reference.
//
// NOT YET CONFIRMED - this is the mod's first flying unit, so some
// things skitter.hjson never had to test are still open:
//   - Whether flying units need any additional sprite (e.g. a shadow
//     sprite cast on the ground) beyond the base body + cell overlay
//     that were sufficient for a ground unit. Two placeholder sprites
//     are provided (buzzer.png, buzzer-cell.png) matching Skitter's
//     set; if a shadow or other flying-specific sprite is required,
//     that will need to be discovered via the same live-load-and-check
//     process used throughout this mod, not guessed here.
//   - mod-units.md describes a splash/puddle damage-over-time effect on
//     impact ("small splash/puddle on impact... optional lingering
//     damage-over-time zone"). NOT implemented here - BasicBulletType
//     (the only confirmed-working bullet type so far) doesn't obviously
//     support this. Left as a plain single-target bullet for now rather
//     than guess at a splash/DoT bullet subtype with no confirmation.
//     Revisit once a splash-capable BulletType is researched/confirmed.
//   - Swarm spawning (2-3 at once) is NOT implemented by this file - it
//     only defines the unit itself. The spawn-side logic (multiple
//     units per trigger) still needs to be built into spawn-hook.js or
//     a parallel hook, per the plan's Task 3D.1 dependency note.
//
// Design intent per mod-units.md: "small flying unit, low health" -
// weaker than Skitter overall, offset by numbers (swarm) and flight
// letting it bypass ground-only defenses. Values below are placeholders
// pending Task 5.2 balance passes, same as every other tuning constant
// in this mod.

type: flying

// --- Movement (confirmed fields) ---
speed: 1.2
accel: 0.5
drag: 0.3
rotateSpeed: 8
hitSize: 6

// --- Combat stats (confirmed fields) ---
health: 18
armor: 0

// --- Behavior flags (confirmed fields) ---
flying: true
targetGround: true
targetAir: false
faceTarget: true
itemCapacity: 0

// --- Weapon: Acid Spit (short-range, fast fire rate, low damage) ---
// No "range" field (confirmed invalid on Weapon - see header). Short
// effective range comes from low bullet speed * lifetime instead.
weapons: [
  {
    name: "buzzer-spit"
    x: 0
    y: 0
    reload: 25
    top: false
    bullet: {
      type: BasicBulletType
      damage: 2
      speed: 3
      lifetime: 10
      width: 3
      height: 4
    }
  }
]
